## 🔧 Code Style & Conventions

### JavaScript/React

**Naming:**
```javascript
// ✅ Components
const RecipeCard = () => { ... }
const ShoppingListItem = () => { ... }

// ✅ Hooks
const useRecipes = () => { ... }
const useScraper = () => { ... }

// ✅ Functions
const fetchRecipeFromUrl = async (url) => { ... }
const calculateNutrition = (ingredients) => { ... }

// ✅ Constants
const DROPBOX_RECIPE_PATH = '/recipes'
const GEMINI_MODEL = 'gemini-2.0-flash-vision'
const CACHE_DURATION_MS = 86400000  // 24h
```

**Comments:**
```javascript
// ✅ Why, not what
// Batch Dropbox requests to avoid rate limiting (300/15min)
const batchRequests = async (items, batchSize = 10) => { ... }

// ❌ Obvious
const x = a + b  // add a and b
```

**Error handling:**
```javascript
// ✅ Specific catch + log
try {
  const data = await fetchRecipeData(url)
  return data
} catch (err) {
  console.error('[fetchRecipeData]', err.message, { url, cause: err.cause })
  throw new Error(`Failed to fetch recipe: ${err.message}`)
}

// ❌ Silent fail
try { ... } catch (e) { }
```

### Worker (Hono)

**Middleware order:**
```javascript
// ✅
app.use(errorHandler)
app.use(authMiddleware)
app.use(rbacMiddleware)
app.route('/api/recipes', recipeRoutes)

// ❌ (RBAC must come after auth)
app.use(rbacMiddleware)
app.use(authMiddleware)
```

**Response format:**
```javascript
// ✅ Consistent JSON
app.get('/api/recipes/:id', async (c) => {
  const recipe = await getRecipe(c.req.param('id'))
  if (!recipe) {
    return c.json({ error: 'Recipe not found' }, 404)
  }
  return c.json({ success: true, data: recipe }, 200)
})

// ❌ Mixed formats
return c.json(recipe)  // no wrapper
```

